<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Amastris</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">died c. 284 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/3rd-century-bce">3rd century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Amastris was a Persian princess, niece of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/darius-iii">Darius III</a>, who married Craterus and then Dionysius, tyrant of Heraclea Pontica. After his death around 305 BCE she ruled Heraclea as regent for their sons, married the Macedonian king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lysimachus">Lysimachus</a> and founded the city of Amastris on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/black-sea">Black Sea</a> coast. She was murdered around 284 BCE.</p></div>
